[2026-05-11T08:59:11.390Z] [INFO] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_75","type":"reasoning","text":"**Evaluating script execution**\n\nI’m considering whether to run `./scripts/check-crystal-syntax.sh`, knowing that it will likely fail due to Crystal not being present. At this point, I think it might be best to not run the command since it’s expected to fail anyway. I could confirm the absence of Crystal with `command -v crystal`. I also need to leave a concise comment on the GitHub PR about this issue, using a heredoc for the command input. It seems acceptable!\n**Considering PR updates**\n\nI’m thinking about using the `--body \"...\"` with quotes, but maybe I'll have to include newlines using `$'...'`. The simpler approach is to just use `gh pr comment 4 --repo lefinepro/cogni --body \"Auto-restart iteration 5...\"`, although I worry about posting a duplicate comment. \n\nThe user asked for an update on the PR, but I might run into permission issues with `gh pr edit 4`. The title is currently \"Feat/acd ml training layer,\" and the body is empty, possibly a placeholder. I’ll have to consider whether I can edit it since I'm not the repo owner.\n**Testing PR edits**\n\nI'm considering testing with `gh pr edit 4 --repo lefinepro/cogni --title \"Feat/acd ml training layer\"`, though I suspect it could succeed or fail without causing harm. However, changing the title might not be the most important focus right now. The main issue is that the PR head is stale. \n\nI could try `gh pr edit 4 --repo lefinepro/cogni --body ...` to overwrite the empty body, but I may run into permission issues. Still, updating the body could be helpful, so it's worth a shot despite past failures."}}
